  "summary": "Package fetches and executes remote install script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js at line 107 runs execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...'), fetching an unpinned install script from a mutable master branch of a repository owned by a different scope (rtk-ai) than the publishing scope (@leejungkiin) and executing it via shell. The same script reads os.homedir(), branches on process.platform, and issues additional HTTPS requests to https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com. The remote install.sh content is not pinned by commit hash and is controlled by a third-party GitHub account; whoever controls that branch can substitute arbitrary shell code that will execute in the installer's environment. bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js additionally combine child_process with outbound HTTPS to external endpoints.",
